==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first and only requirement, there's not much effort required, as Shrimpo is the cheapest Toon ever in the game. You only need 100 {{II|Ichor|name=true}} to buy him, so you can go on a simple solo run until [[Floor]] 3 and get 100 Ichor.

==Strategies==
Shrimpo is a special [[Toon]], having atrocious [[Stats]], with all of them being 1{{Star}}, especially his [[Stealth]], which is '''-99''', which is the second lowest Stealth in the game. With that being said, you are advised to '''''avoid playing as him for general play.''''' 

As the description of his [[Ability]] states, only play as him if you are looking for a challenge. In case if one actually wants to play as the character, whether for special runs, just for fun, to complete his mastery or to get {{TTI|Hissy Fit|name=true}}, here are some tips, tricks, and strategies to do at least decently, as extreme Stealth and patience is key.

Since [[Twisteds]] will spot him easily, there is very little room for error, and getting chased usually means your run will end early. As such, you may have to wait things out until you are absolutely certain the situation is safe to proceed.

[[Items]] can also help greatly as Shrimpo's speed is easily one of his biggest hindrances, and Trinkets can help offset (however, small) some of his drawbacks. In this sense, Shrimpo can be a great character to start learning the game with, as mistakes cost him more than they would any other Toon, even if some [[Toons]] have 1 {{Star}} Movement Speed.

Be careful with faster Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Toodles|name=true}} since her Speed will overwhelm you. Twisted Toodles' chase speed is the same as Shrimpo's run speed. It's best to stay out of any Twisteds' way as they are likely to spot you. If you do get caught up in the line-sight of a Twisted, looping around any structure not connected to a wall is a good idea as it will allow you to stay out of sight while also running too far away.

Shrimpo may find use from extracting machines near the [[Elevator]] as on earlier [[Floors]] with good timing you should finish up around when most other machines are complete giving you a good head start on getting to the Elevator, something that is very due advantageous to the danger [[Panic Mode]] gives to Shrimpo, though with {{TI|Vanity Mirror|name=true}} equipped, this can be avoided. It's also easier if you purchase the {{II|Valve|name=false}} Item from the Pre-game UI to even finish the first Machine.

One very applicable skill Shrimpo has is watching {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}}. Because Shrimpo isn't exactly the best at Extraction, and is nearly incapable of kiting, leaving him to make sure Glisten doesn't become hostile whilst the other Toons handle bigger problems is a smart idea.

Of course, you'll need to be told by your teammates when to get away from Glisten and when they are on last, as he immediately becomes hostile when Panic Mode happens.

Despite the atrocity that is Shrimpo and his general gameplay, there is one purpose that he can do better than any other Toon in the game, a strategy unique to him only, which is magnetism. Shrimpo's -99 Stealth means that he can be spotted from very far away, and cannot have aggro taken off him (unless from {{CI|Blot|name=true}}'s Ability), which can be used to his advantage, as shown in the example scenarios below:
*If a distractor is struggling to deal with long-ranged Twisteds, Shrimpo can take aggro off of the distractor from really far away right before the Twisted launches their attack, (if you time it correctly) because of how far you'd be, you will remain in safe distances and get much longer time to escape the attack. While this sounds niche at first, there is much more to magnet distraction.
*If Shrimpo sees a Toon with low Stealth, like {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, especially one with bad mobility, Shrimpo can act as a permanent bodyguard as even a Brightney using an {{II|Air Horn|name=false}} will have more Stealth than Shrimpo, but do remember that because of the fact Shrimpo has terrible mobility as well, it is important to use the {{TI|Pop Pack|name=true}} with a mobility Trinket, (or 2 mobility Trinkets, though it might not be as effective), for this.
*If there are Twisteds near the Elevator during Panic Mode, Shrimpo can aggro them to him and return inside the Elevator, surprisingly enough the Twisteds will be frozen all grouped in one place, which unless dealing with Twisted Toodles, means you are basically stunning the Twisteds.
*This also unlocks the ability to distract during Panic Mode by using some {{II|Pop|name=false}} from your Pop Pack combined with the Vanity Mirror making you fast enough to outrun most Twisteds while keeping your stamina high.
*This strategy removes the need to take items on the floor, which your teammates could want, and removes the need of extracting, which is something your teammates can do more effectively than you could, but gives you a special strategy that could even save your distractor.

If you follow all these tips right, Shrimpo will start feeling like a Toon with a unique playstyle, as Shrimpo can save Toons low on stamina about to get comboed to death by Twisteds, even if they have low Stealth, as he has the lowest Stealth in the game.

